  "id": "correct-rejection",
  "term": "correct rejection",
  "definition": "Correct rejection is a recognition-memory response in which a person correctly judges that a test item was not previously studied or presented. In false-memory research, it can also refer specifically to correctly rejecting a related lure, meaning a new item that feels familiar because it is linked to studied material.",
